{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 1 RCA — confirmed before repair\n\nProven mechanism: the batched overlap judge constructs a native structured RunRequest without overlap-local output, retry, or elapsed-time budgets (src/rebar/llm/overlap/judge.py:173-182). It therefore inherits the generic 16,000-token / 600-second per-request settings (src/rebar/llm/config.py:117-128,478-480), and native structured validation may make OUTPUT_RETRIES+1 = 3 sequential generations before judge_batch regains control and safely abstains (src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:225-286; judge.py:182,199-201). The generic timeout applies per provider request, not to the whole advisory episode, so it does not prevent three long generations.\n\nDiscriminating runtime proof: two live failures took 241.1s and 216.3s, produced malformed EOF responses of 47,973 and 21,351 characters with repeated candidate_id, exhausted both output retries, and then safely abstained. A deterministic FunctionModel probe through the real judge/runner path recorded max_tokens=16000 on all three baseline attempts and preserved all-candidate abstention. Holding the same malformed payload and 50ms generation delay constant, current retry policy made 3 calls in 0.178s; setting output retries to zero made 1 call in 0.062s with the same abstention. Applying output_token_limit=1024 alone changed the effective cap to 1024 but still made 3 native structured attempts, proving a token cap alone is insufficient. A 40,020-character completed payload was accepted by the current unconstrained candidate_id contract; a temporary max-length validator rejected it only after all bytes existed, proving schema tightening alone cannot contain latency.\n\nAlternatives ruled down: batch size six is not independently sufficient—the c403 live-provider evidence successfully completed repeated six-candidate runs (599 output tokens)—and candidate-id echo is an observed model-side structured-output-collapse trigger/amplifier, not the executable containment defect. The parsimonious code defect is the absence of operation-local token + retry + elapsed-time bounds before graceful abstention.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. Closed story 9022-d3e3-e97f-47e3 explicitly specifies a bounded pairwise classifier and timeout/error/malformed-output abstention; accepted ADR 0086 requires an advisory-only graceful skip. Multi-minute, multiply retried abstention violates that documented intent."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786251659444495001,"uuid":"e11a6fd2-e34b-4e6b-9e44-eda00c68c735"}